.SH "NAME"
econf\&.NewKeyFile, econf\&.NewKeyFileWithOptions, econf\&.NewIniFile \- create a new econf\&.File object

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
import "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/bindings/go/econf"
.fi
.ft
.sp
.nf
\fBfunc NewKeyFile(delimiter, comment byte) (*econf\&.File, error)\fR

\fBfunc NewKeyFileWithOptions(options string) (*econf\&.File, error)\fR

\fBfunc NewIniFile() (*econf\&.File, error)\fR
.fi

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
These functions create a new, empty
\fBeconf\&.File\fR
object\&. The returned
\fI*File\fR
should be released with
\fB(*File)\&.Close\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_File_Close\fR(3)) once it is no longer needed; typically with
\fCdefer f\&.Close()\fR
right after a successful call\&.

.PP
\fBNewKeyFile\fR
takes the
\fIdelimiter\fR
character used to separate keys from values (e\&.g\&.,
\*(Aq=\*(Aq
or
\*(Aq \*(Aq), and the
\fIcomment\fR
character used to mark the beginning of a comment line (e\&.g\&.,
\*(Aq#\*(Aq
or
\*(Aq;\*(Aq)\&.

.PP
\fBNewKeyFileWithOptions\fR
creates a new, empty
\fBeconf\&.File\fR
configured by a
";"\-separated
"key=value"
\fIoptions\fR
string (e\&.g\&.,
"DEFAULT_DELIMITER==;DEFAULT_COMMENT=#")\&. See
\fBeconf_newKeyFile_with_options\fR(3)
for the full list of supported options\&.

.PP
\fBNewIniFile\fR
creates a new
\fBeconf\&.File\fR
in INI format
(\*(Aq=\*(Aq
delimiter,
\*(Aq#\*(Aq
comments) and takes no arguments\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
On success, these functions return a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.File\fR
and a
\fInil\fR
error\&.

.PP
On failure, they return
\fInil\fR
and a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.Error\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3))\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoMem\fR
.RS 4
          Insufficient memory to allocate the new
\fBeconf\&.File\fR
object\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrOptionNotFound\fR
.RS 4
          \fBNewKeyFileWithOptions\fR
only: an unknown option was given in
\fIoptions\fR\&.
.RE

.SH "EXAMPLE"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 1
.\}
.nf

package main

import (
    "log"

    "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/bindings/go/econf"
)

func main() {
    f, err := econf\&.NewIniFile()
    if err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
    defer f\&.Close()

    if err := f\&.SetString("main", "greeting", "hello"); err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
}

.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

